+**Honor the lane contract before the artifact checklist.** A read-only dogfood
+or stand-in lane must not modify source, board files, dogfood logs, docs, or
+skills, even though the normal dogfood loop asks a committing lane to leave
+knowledge behind. Park the run record in the resolved DuckBrain project
+namespace instead, then read it back and report the key; return findings as
+row-ready evidence without minting or appending task ids. Resolve THAT target
+before writing: list the candidate namespaces and read the lane's own prior
+records, then copy the key SHAPE its earlier ticks used (a project-scoped
+`/dogfood/<date>/<slug>` vs a lane-scoped `/…/dogfood/tick-<date>-<slug>`) — an
+invented-but-plausible key silently splits the history, so a reader who searches
+the namespace the lane normally writes to finds half the runs. Pass the resolved
+DuckBrain namespace explicitly on every read and write; an omitted namespace can
+silently query the default namespace, and a schema-shaped write still needs its
+required domain, attributes, and embedding text fields. Verify the
+credential by READING first: `Unauthorized: Invalid API key` (401) means the
+token is wrong, `not found` (404) means it authenticated — the newest
